{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const useForm: UseFormHook<DefaultVueFormComponentMap>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/vue-form/src/VueForm/useForm.public.ts#L51","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/vue-form/src/VueForm/useForm.public.ts:51"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Vue form whose instance and lifecycle are owned by the current\ncomponent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" establish the initial state and inferred form value type. To\nupdate the existing form after creation, pass a reactive options object;\ntracked changes are applied without replacing the form instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call this during the component's setup phase. The form mounts with the\ncomponent and is cleaned up when the component unmounts."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: { name: '' },\n  onSubmit: ({ value }) => saveProfile(value),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Vue form API with typed field, subscription, and form-group\ncomponents attached."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst useForm: UseFormHook<DefaultVueFormComponentMap>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/vue-form/src/VueForm/useForm.public.ts:51](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/vue-form/src/VueForm/useForm.public.ts#L51)\n\nCreates a Vue form whose instance and lifecycle are owned by the current\ncomponent.\n\n`defaultValues` establish the initial state and inferred form value type. To\nupdate the existing form after creation, pass a reactive options object;\ntracked changes are applied without replacing the form instance.\n\nCall this during the component's setup phase. The form mounts with the\ncomponent and is cleaned up when the component unmounts.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: { name: '' },\n  onSubmit: ({ value }) => saveProfile(value),\n})\n```\n\n## Returns\n\nThe Vue form API with typed field, subscription, and form-group\ncomponents attached.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useForm\ntitle: useForm\n---\n\n```ts\nconst useForm: UseFormHook<DefaultVueFormComponentMap>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/vue-form/src/VueForm/useForm.public.ts:51](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/vue-form/src/VueForm/useForm.public.ts#L51)\n\nCreates a Vue form whose instance and lifecycle are owned by the current\ncomponent.\n\n`defaultValues` establish the initial state and inferred form value type. To\nupdate the existing form after creation, pass a reactive options object;\ntracked changes are applied without replacing the form instance.\n\nCall this during the component's setup phase. The form mounts with the\ncomponent and is cleaned up when the component unmounts.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: { name: '' },\n  onSubmit: ({ value }) => saveProfile(value),\n})\n```\n\n## Returns\n\nThe Vue form API with typed field, subscription, and form-group\ncomponents attached.\n"}
